The nine P0s reduce to one failure mode with two faces. **Truncation with a direction** — three load-bearing citations each stop one clause before the complication, and every omitted clause cuts the same way (*Med.* 8.1 turns to "and be content"; 5.9 to "be content if the greater part"; HA 21.4's five days of mourning stops right before HA 21.5 explains that the games of Jupiter were running). The page is doing a more careful version of what it condemns the Stoicism industry for. **Attribution that fails a citation check** — the designated hostile witness is one sentence welded from two HA documents thirteen years apart, with the colourful half spoken by a man five years dead at the event it's dated to; the origin claim never names Junius Rusticus and hands Fronto the credit by referent; the Lyon paragraph calls a contemporary letter "Eusebius, writing more than a century later" and omits *EH* 5.1.47, inside a sentence promising not to smooth over.

Three findings I verified independently rather than taking on the reviewers' word: Epictetus *Discourses* 3.10.2–3 really does prescribe the nightly audit ("Blame what is wrong, in what is right rejoice"), which is what makes the page's stated clincher type the school rather than the man — and supplies a better argument in its place; `enneagram-type-1.md:138,140` confirms the site's own wing definitions turn on direction-of-correction, not warmth, so the page argues 1w9 in the body and asserts 1w2 in the Rabbit Hole; and Marcus did endow four chairs of philosophy at Athens in 176, which makes "built no school" need three more words.

**The constraint you should know about:** I ran `blog-lint.sh` — the draft is at **4,494 body words against a 4,500 ceiling**. The P0 set is ~+85 gross. I've included a word ledger with named funding cuts (~−106 available, mostly the two Ariston repetitions two perspectives independently want gone). That funds all nine P0s, but **not** P1-01 and P1-02 — the genre/self-selection objection and Med. 11.18's self-reproach line, each flagged by three perspectives, ~+95 together. Those are the page's answer to its own strongest objection. That's a ceiling-exception call for you, not the editor's, so the brief escalates rather than either dropping them or silently exceeding.

**Most important protected hit:** *"That still made him hard to be around, and Fronto was right to push."* Four perspectives name it; the critic says if one sentence survives revision, it's this one. It must stay adjacent to the Book 1 debt-ledger paragraph — separated, the explanation becomes an excuse. Close second and more fragile: the edition-of-record attributions (Loeb 1919/1920, Long 1862). They're the likeliest casualty of a word-starved pass and they're the reason every quotation here is checkable forever.
